{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917463157},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a data question that requires:\n1. Total number of farmers markets in the US\n2. Total US population from the census file\n3. Calculate the ratio: farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nAccording to the AGENTS.md instructions, I should:\n1. First check if there's a xorq catalog and semantic models\n2. Orient using xorq_semantic_models and xorq_catalog_list_aliases\n3. Only ingest sources if they're not already in the catalog\n4. Use xorq_select to compute values\n5. Declare obligations for every number\n6. Call xorq_verify to verify the answer\n7. Check lineage with xorq_check_lineage\n\nLet me start by checking what's in the catalog, then if needed, ingest the data sources.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the number of farmers markets per 100,000 US residents. Let me start by checking the xorq catalog for existing data."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_018g125LgzDuPS8rczxEBiVM","name":"xorq_catalog_info","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01J11pcAzP8TQSpSd38t97Aw","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01WEzmLQYEA9cgf9XY1CQjpA","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","u